up-milkdrop-pack @VERSION@
==========================

MilkDrop presets for the Universal Proxy "MilkDrop" TV display mode
(github.com/bbangert/universal_proxy). The device downloads this archive
on first use, checks its SHA-256 against the value compiled into the
firmware and extracts it to /data/milkdrop/@VERSION@/.

Layout (see c_src/milkdrop_renderer/README.md in universal_proxy):

  manifest.json        preset list, tags and Raspberry Pi 3 hints (format 1)
  presets/             the .milk files; presets/high_frequency/ holds the
                       fast-flashing ones, which stay off unless enabled
  textures/            the textures the presets sample, plus MilkDrop's own
                       set as the random-texture pool (lowercase names)
  shaders/<key>.glsl   warp/comp shaders pre-translated to GLSL ES 1.00
  README, NOTICE       this file and the provenance and licence notes

Contents: @PRESETS@ presets (@HIGH_FREQUENCY@ under high_frequency/, @EXTREME@ of
those under high_frequency/extreme/), @TEXTURES@ textures, @SHADERS@
pre-translated shaders.

How it was built (tools/milkdrop_pack in universal_proxy @ @APP_COMMIT@):

  - presets: @ZIP_NAME@ (sha256 @ZIP_SHA@); preview
    thumbnails dropped; file names normalised (ASCII, single spaces,
    trimmed); contents unchanged;
  - excluded: @EXCLUDED@ presets (see NOTICE for the reasons);
  - textures: projectM presets-milkdrop-texture-pack @ @TEXTURE_COMMIT@;
    textures larger than @MAX_TEXTURE_PX@ px downscaled to fit;
  - shaders: projectM-pretranslate-presets --target es100 from
    bbangert/projectm @ @PROJECTM_COMMIT@ (the commit milkdrop_renderer
    pins), with textures/ in place;
  - brightness screen: each preset rendered @BRIGHT_FRAMES@ frames at @BRIGHT_SIZE@ with
    synthetic music on a host reference renderer; presets with more than
    @BRIGHT_EXCLUDE_PCT@% of the picture saturated (any channel >= 250) over frames
    @BRIGHT_FROM@-@BRIGHT_FRAMES@ are left out as whiteouts;
  - rpi3 hints: @RPI3_SOURCE@.
